course: dictionary
lesson: 4727
title: Hopscotch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hopscotch is a children's game played on numbered squares drawn on the ground. You throw a small stone or marker into a square, then hop through the squares to pick it up. Here it is a noun for the game itself.
explain: Use the words around it to understand. «Mrs Platt at number 22 shuts her curtains when kids say hello and rings the council about hopscotch, so the kids play in the park instead.» The kids want to play a game outdoors, and the park is where they go, so hopscotch is something you play outside.
explain: Other languages have their own names for it. «klAsyky means hopscotch, drawn on the pavement with chalk.» «La marelle ("la ma-REL") is hopscotch, and children often call out the number of each square as they land.» The words are different, but the game is the same.
fact: Hopscotch is a children's game with numbered squares drawn on the ground.
fact: You throw a small stone or marker into a square, then hop through the squares to pick it up.
fact: Hopscotch squares are often painted or drawn with chalk on playgrounds and pavements.
fact: Hopscotch helps balance and counting, because children say the numbers as they hop.
fact: In maths lessons, a hopscotch grid can be used to practise number order and skip counting.
exercise: «Mrs Platt ... rings the council about hopscotch, so the kids play in the park instead.» Where do the kids play? | *In the park | Inside the council office | On the pavement outside her curtains | On Mrs Platt's doorstep
exercise: In hopscotch, what do you throw into a square? | *A small stone or marker | A skipping rope | A ball | A piece of chalk
exercise: «La marelle» is another name for which game? | Ball games | Hide and seek | *Hopscotch | Skipping
test: In hopscotch, what do children often say as they land? | Goodbye | Hello | *The number of each square | The names of their friends
test: Which word means a skipping rope? | cache-cache | m'yach | *skAkalka | klAsyky
exam: Why is hopscotch useful in maths lessons? | It teaches children how to cook | It teaches children to paint pictures | *It helps children practise number order and skip counting | It is only a game for hiding
